{
  "id": "YuGM6hvLvIvSCnSk",
  "name": "SecOps — Alert Triage (multi-agent)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### SecOps — Orchestrated Alert Triage\nA guarded, multi-agent SOC pipeline.\n\n**1. Guardrails (input):** the alert text is attacker-influenced. Screens for prompt-injection (jailbreak) + leaked secrets before any LLM sees it. Flagged → quarantine.\n**2. Orchestrator agent:** calls the **Triage Agent** (sub-workflow) to get a verdict, then — only for confirmed high/critical — calls the **Response Planner** (sub-workflow) for a containment plan. Both ground in IR runbooks (RAG).\n**3. Severity gate → HITL:** high/critical routes through a **form approval** before any write.\n**4. Write:** on approval, open a **Better Stack** incident (on-call / IRM system of record). Critical severity also triggers call + SMS + critical push.\n\n**Wire-up:** OpenAI, urlscan.io, Pinecone (secops-kb) on the sub-workflows; a **Better Stack API token** (httpBearerAuth) on the write. HITL is credential-free (n8n form).",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky_overview",
      "name": "Sticky: Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
