    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Triage this alert and, if warranted, plan a response.\n\nType: {{ $('Incoming alert').item.json.alert_type }}\nIndicator: {{ $('Incoming alert').item.json.indicator }}\nSource: {{ $('Incoming alert').item.json.source }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are the SecOps triage orchestrator. Coordinate two specialist sub-agents exposed as tools:\n\n1. ALWAYS call `triage_agent` first, passing the alert type, indicator, and source. It returns a structured verdict (malicious/suspicious/benign) and severity, grounded in IR runbooks.\n2. IF the verdict is 'malicious' or 'suspicious' AND severity is 'high' or 'critical', call `response_planner` with the verdict, severity, alert type, indicator, and the triage rationale. It returns a runbook-grounded containment plan. If not escalating, do NOT call it and leave containment_steps empty.\n3. Return a single combined structured decision. Preserve the sub-agents' verdict/severity exactly — do not override them. Cite any runbook the sub-agents referenced in the rationale.\n\nBe conservative: when evidence is mixed, prefer 'suspicious' over 'benign'.",
          "returnIntermediateSteps": true
        }
      },
